                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "236692790",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199195512395",
                            "num_reviews": 33,
                            "playtime_forever": 7,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 7,
                            "deck_playtime_at_review": 7,
                            "last_played": 1790907367
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is far and away one of the most unique games I’ve ever played, likely because it was made—conceptualized, developed, and scored—by a single person. I already played through most of it on Nintendo Switch, and when I saw that it was on such a deep discount on Steam, I knew I had to pick it up. \n\nThe simplest way to describe it is as a top-down F-Zero-like with shoot-em-up mechanics and an Ancient Greek flare (it’s more or less a loose retelling of the Odyssey). The driving feels fast and slick, with that same slightly slippery feeling of the original F-Zero—not enough to feel miserable, but enough to make you feel smart for getting the hang of it. The tracks are very well-designed, and the soundtrack and sound design in general is quite memorable. The upgrades can radically change how you play based on which one you favor, but never feel overpowered. \n\nThere are a couple of questionable choices in my opinion, such as making one boss fight an arena instead of a track, and there is a definite difficulty spike. But the sheer uniqueness of the game combined with the excellent driving feel and upgrade implementation make this a true hidden gem. And at the current sale price of $1.29, it’s a must-buy.",
